WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.710 --> 00:00:04.020
Game of Thrones Season 6 Episode 9 let’s
have a look.

00:00:04.020 --> 00:00:05.970
Meereen is under siege by the slavers.

00:00:05.970 --> 00:00:09.780
Daenerys speaks with Tyrion and he says the
city is doing quite well, apart for the whole

00:00:09.780 --> 00:00:12.260
being bombarded with flaming rocks bit.

00:00:12.260 --> 00:00:16.250
Dany is unimpressed and declares she will
crucify the slavers, kill all their soldiers,

00:00:16.250 --> 00:00:21.699
and destroy their cities, she is embracing
the role of a violent vengeful dragon queen.

00:00:21.699 --> 00:00:25.919
Tyrion plays the angel on her shoulder, suggesting
that wiping out whole cities might not be

00:00:25.919 --> 00:00:27.279
the right thing to do.

00:00:27.279 --> 00:00:31.579
He reminds her of the madness and the cruelty
of her father Aerys, and tells her about his

00:00:31.579 --> 00:00:34.670
plan to destroy King’s Landing with wildfire.

00:00:34.670 --> 00:00:38.829
This is an important warning for Dany – hopefully
she’ll avoid becoming a terrible tyrant

00:00:38.829 --> 00:00:39.829
like her father.

00:00:39.829 --> 00:00:43.960
But this is also yet another hint that the
wildfire beneath King’s Landing is still

00:00:43.960 --> 00:00:49.440
down there, just waiting for a mad queen to
set it off and burn the city…

00:00:49.440 --> 00:00:51.590
So Dany and co go chat with the slavers.

00:00:51.590 --> 00:00:55.159
They demand that Dany surrender, but they
seem to have forgotten that Dany has a gigantic

00:00:55.159 --> 00:01:01.649
bloody dragon, scratch that, three gigantic
dragons, who fly in the sky and the CGI looks

00:01:01.649 --> 00:01:02.649
sick.

00:01:02.649 --> 00:01:06.790
Meanwhile, the Sons of the Harpy are up to
their usual shenanigans, slaughtering civilians,

00:01:06.790 --> 00:01:10.310
so Dany’s Dothraki with Daario ride in to
sweep them away.

00:01:10.310 --> 00:01:13.280
The whole thing with the Sons of the Harpy
has been weird this season.

00:01:13.280 --> 00:01:17.180
In Episode 1, there seemed to be a set-up
for a mystery to uncover who their leader

00:01:17.180 --> 00:01:21.659
is , but that never really went anywhere – apparently
it’s just been the slavers funding them

00:01:21.659 --> 00:01:23.920
all along, which hardly a surprise.

00:01:23.920 --> 00:01:28.610
lf you wanna put on your tinfoil hat, it could
be that Varys has secretly been behind the

00:01:28.610 --> 00:01:33.440
Harpy all this time, as a way of pushing Dany
to leave Meereen and go to Westeros sooner.

00:01:33.440 --> 00:01:37.930
And it is curious that Varys has never once
met Dany this whole season.

00:01:37.930 --> 00:01:40.399
But it’s probably nothing.

00:01:40.399 --> 00:01:44.590
So Dany’s dragons fly around and burn a
slaver ship – they leave most of the ships

00:01:44.590 --> 00:01:48.930
untouched, cause Dany wants to capture the
slaver navy, not wipe it out – and this

00:01:48.930 --> 00:01:54.320
is really first time we’ve seen adult dragons
used in war, and they do look so destructive

00:01:54.320 --> 00:01:58.149
and unstoppable – just imagine what these
monsters would do to the armies of Westeros

00:01:58.149 --> 00:02:00.759
– hopefully, we’ll soon see.

00:02:00.759 --> 00:02:02.369
But yeah the slavers are basically screwed.

00:02:02.369 --> 00:02:06.310
So Grey Worm lets their soldiers go free,
but Missandei says that one of slavers must

00:02:06.310 --> 00:02:07.310
die.

00:02:07.310 --> 00:02:11.670
The two highborn guys gang up on the low-born,
say to kill him, but in a kinda King Solomon

00:02:11.670 --> 00:02:16.330
fashion, Grey Worm kills the upper two, and
lets the lowborn, Yezzan, go to warn his slaver

00:02:16.330 --> 00:02:20.130
friends of the power of Daenerys Targaryen.

00:02:20.130 --> 00:02:23.750
Over in Westeros, outside Winterfell, the
Starks confront the Boltons.

00:02:23.750 --> 00:02:28.830
Ramsay brings Lords Umber and Karstark, while
Jon brings Sansa and Davos and Tormund and

00:02:28.830 --> 00:02:31.450
Lyanna, so it’s pretty clear who’s got
the cooler squad.

00:02:31.450 --> 00:02:34.990
The two sides threaten and taunt each other,
it doesn’t really go anywhere, just setting

00:02:34.990 --> 00:02:37.530
the stage for the fight that is to come.

00:02:37.530 --> 00:02:41.471
Back at camp, the Starks strategise, and things
don’t look good, they just don’t have

00:02:41.471 --> 00:02:44.740
enough men, but they devise a plan as best
they can.

00:02:44.740 --> 00:02:48.351
Sansa gets mad at Jon for not asking her what
to do, so he asks her what to do, and she

00:02:48.351 --> 00:02:49.930
says she doesn’t know what to do.

00:02:49.930 --> 00:02:54.490
But she does give him some really good advice,
she says that Ramsay toys with people, baits

00:02:54.490 --> 00:02:59.130
them and traps them, she warns him not to
do what Ramsay wants him to do – which comes

00:02:59.130 --> 00:03:00.380
up later on.

00:03:00.380 --> 00:03:02.160
Then we see Davos talking with Tormund.

00:03:02.160 --> 00:03:06.350
They find common ground in that they both
served failed kings – Davos served King

00:03:06.350 --> 00:03:09.950
Stannis, and Tormund served the King-Beyond-the-Wall
Mance Rayder.

00:03:09.950 --> 00:03:14.850
They figure Jon might be a better man to follow
cause he’s not a king – funny thing is

00:03:14.850 --> 00:03:18.840
that there’s lots of foreshadowing in the
books and the show that Jon may become a king

00:03:18.840 --> 00:03:21.590
– maybe sooner than we think.

00:03:21.590 --> 00:03:23.260
But then Jon visits Melisandre.

00:03:23.260 --> 00:03:27.290
They chat about her god, and while Mel’s
pretty sure that god has as plan for us all,

00:03:27.290 --> 00:03:29.290
she says it might not be a nice one.

00:03:29.290 --> 00:03:33.950
There’s a sense of resignation here, a feeling
that everything might go terribly wrong but

00:03:33.950 --> 00:03:36.810
that there’s nothing anyone can do to stop
it.

00:03:36.810 --> 00:03:40.910
Jon tells Mel not to bring him back if he
dies in battle.

00:03:40.910 --> 00:03:43.830
It would have been nice to have seen more
of Mel this season.

00:03:43.830 --> 00:03:48.170
Episode 1 had that revelation of her ancient
age, it seemed to set up for some exploration

00:03:48.170 --> 00:03:51.020
of her character, but we never really got
any.

00:03:51.020 --> 00:03:55.250
We do know, though, that she’ll have a role
in Episode 10, because when Davos goes a walking,

00:03:55.250 --> 00:03:59.790
he finds the wooden stag he carved for Shireen,
the little girl who was burned by Mel last

00:03:59.790 --> 00:04:00.790
season.

00:04:00.790 --> 00:04:04.820
Davos loved Shireen like a daughter, he’s
gonna want justice for her, which means Mel

00:04:04.820 --> 00:04:07.710
might face dire consequences.

00:04:07.710 --> 00:04:10.500
Back in Meereen, Yara and Theon arrive to
meet Daenerys.

00:04:10.500 --> 00:04:13.871
It would have been cool to have gotten some
shots of the ironborn actually sailing in,

00:04:13.871 --> 00:04:17.510
in the midst of battle, as is happening in
the books, but whatever, the Greyjoys are

00:04:17.510 --> 00:04:22.060
now here, and we start with Tyrion attacking
Theon for having been rude to him in Season

00:04:22.060 --> 00:04:26.759
1, which is weird, cause it was actually mostly
Tyrion being rude to Theon, so maybe Tyrion

00:04:26.759 --> 00:04:28.570
just has a bad memory.

00:04:28.570 --> 00:04:32.949
Dany complains about their respective shitty
dads – Aerys for Dany, Tywin for Tyrion,

00:04:32.949 --> 00:04:36.960
Balon for Yara and Theon – and there’s
a strong feminist undertone here.

00:04:36.960 --> 00:04:43.169
Between Dany and Yara and Ellaria and Sansa,
women are now taking power in a usually male-dominated

00:04:43.169 --> 00:04:44.169
Westeros.

00:04:44.169 --> 00:04:48.360
Yara hits on Dany, which gives the shippers
and fanficcers something to squee about.

00:04:48.360 --> 00:04:52.850
And ultimately they agree to work together
– Dany will help Yara take the Iron Islands,

00:04:52.850 --> 00:04:57.900
and Yara will help Dany take Westeros . Dany’s
one condition is that the ironborn stop raiding

00:04:57.900 --> 00:05:01.880
and reaving and stealing shit from the other
kingdoms, which is not a super realistic demand,

00:05:01.880 --> 00:05:06.830
cause as Yara says, that’s the ironborn
way of life, can they really be expected to

00:05:06.830 --> 00:05:09.370
suddenly reinvent their whole culture?

00:05:09.370 --> 00:05:14.009
Dany has the same problem with the Dothraki
– when these guys war, they rape and pillage,

00:05:14.009 --> 00:05:18.189
and Dany can’t reasonably expect that to
quickly or easily change.

00:05:18.189 --> 00:05:21.979
When Dany invades Westeros, she’s bringing
foreign sellswords, she’s bringing Dothraki

00:05:21.979 --> 00:05:26.319
screamers, she’s bringing ironborn reavers
– and some, she assumes, are good people.

00:05:26.319 --> 00:05:30.139
But if she’s expecting all of these groups
to happily get along with the Westerosi after

00:05:30.139 --> 00:05:33.039
she takes over she’s gonna have a bad time.

00:05:33.039 --> 00:05:35.930
Back in Westeros, the Stark and Bolton armies
face off.

00:05:35.930 --> 00:05:41.969
Ramsay uses Rickon as bait to draw out Jon,
and Jon, being a brave hero and a bloody idiot

00:05:41.969 --> 00:05:45.889
who didn’t listen to Sansa, rides right
into Ramsay’s trap, only for Rickon to get

00:05:45.889 --> 00:05:49.970
hit at the last minute with an Olympic-level
archery shot from Ramsay.

00:05:49.970 --> 00:05:54.389
Rickon really didn’t do much this season,
didn’t have a single line – just turned

00:05:54.389 --> 00:05:57.639
up, looked sad then died, but there’s still
a lot of hope that he’ll be awesome in the

00:05:57.639 --> 00:06:03.280
books – he’s apparently hanging with Osha
and Shaggy on an island of cannibals and unicorns.

00:06:03.280 --> 00:06:07.159
But yeah now Jon’s stuck out in the open,
so Ramsay activates his trap card, sending

00:06:07.159 --> 00:06:11.469
his cavalry out to squash Jon – and giving
us easily one of the coolest shots in the

00:06:11.469 --> 00:06:17.409
series with Jon standing and facing the enemy,
looking ready for a second death – but the

00:06:17.409 --> 00:06:21.221
Stark forces ride up behind him and then we
get this crazy intense combat scene, with

00:06:21.221 --> 00:06:25.370
horses and soldiers and swords and blood and
mud flying every which way.

00:06:25.370 --> 00:06:30.599
It’s pretty stunning – the violence is
brutal and chaotic and exciting and sickening

00:06:30.599 --> 00:06:31.630
all at once.

00:06:31.630 --> 00:06:36.659
Ramsay keeps firing arrows, Davos and Smalljon
join in, and the bodies pile up, until Ramsay

00:06:36.659 --> 00:06:41.219
surrounds the Stark forces with Bolton shields
– he has sprung another trap.

00:06:41.219 --> 00:06:46.789
As the Boltons close in, Wun Wun does a surprisingly
poor job of breaking free, Tormund Mike Tysons

00:06:46.789 --> 00:06:51.210
Smalljon, and things start getting a bit too
cosy, with Jon almost crushed by the mass

00:06:51.210 --> 00:06:56.169
of bodies in a shot reminiscent of Daenerys
at the end of Season 3, but without the uncomfortable

00:06:56.169 --> 00:06:57.169
racial imagery.

00:06:57.169 --> 00:07:01.140
Then when all hope seems lost, the knights
of the Vale ride in to save the day, like

00:07:01.140 --> 00:07:05.099
the Rohirrim at Helm’s Deep, except instead
of being led by Gandalf, they’re led by

00:07:05.099 --> 00:07:08.840
Littlefinger, a decidedly less trustworthy
ally.

00:07:08.840 --> 00:07:13.280
Ramsay retreats to Winterfell, Jon gives chase,
Wun Wun breaks the gate, and is killed by

00:07:13.280 --> 00:07:14.860
an arrow from Ramsay.

00:07:14.860 --> 00:07:19.740
Which is actually super tragic because as
far as we know, Wun Wun is the last of his

00:07:19.740 --> 00:07:20.740
species.

00:07:20.740 --> 00:07:24.529
Along with the children of the forest, this
is the second apparent extinction of the season,

00:07:24.529 --> 00:07:29.219
the two native inhabitants of Westeros are
now as far we know, totally gone.

00:07:29.219 --> 00:07:33.719
There are bits about this in the books, it’s
like a Lord of the Rings type deal with the

00:07:33.719 --> 00:07:38.900
old races of magic and nature disappearing
and being replaced by “the world that men

00:07:38.900 --> 00:07:44.430
have made” . Here’s a sad little song
sung by wildlings eulogising the giants.

00:07:44.430 --> 00:07:48.939
So Jon punches Ramsay in the face twenty one
times, and Ramsay somehow not only survives

00:07:48.939 --> 00:07:52.910
but is left with a face that still looks like
a face – just got some red paint on it,

00:07:52.910 --> 00:07:57.750
which feels kinda silly, but regardless, the
Starks now have Winterfell, which pleases

00:07:57.750 --> 00:08:10.960
Mel because she foresaw this long ago . 
What Mel doesn’t know is that Davos is eyeing

00:08:10.960 --> 00:08:12.740
her – he wants justice for Shireen.

00:08:12.740 --> 00:08:16.839
And there’s a really cool way this could
go down – it may be that Mel will be put

00:08:16.839 --> 00:08:23.009
to death for the murder of Shireen, so Jon
might execute Mel, and if he does, his sword

00:08:23.009 --> 00:08:28.069
may be set alight with Mel’s inner fire,
transforming it into Lightbringer , the flaming

00:08:28.069 --> 00:08:32.700
sword of Azor Ahai, the hero prophesied to
save the world from the white walkers.

00:08:32.700 --> 00:08:37.650
This might not be likely, at least in the
show, but it would be pretty sick.

00:08:37.650 --> 00:08:41.330
The Starks have recovered Rickon’s body
– even though those cavalry charges should

00:08:41.330 --> 00:08:45.440
have reduced it to bloody slurry – and Jon
says he’ll bury the body in the Winterfell

00:08:45.440 --> 00:08:49.940
crypts – and this is exciting cause there’s
heaps of mystery and foreshadowing surrounding

00:08:49.940 --> 00:08:54.709
the crypts – Ned and Bran and Rickon and
especially Jon all have dreams of the crypts

00:08:54.709 --> 00:09:00.200
, fans believe there’s some secret deep
inside relating to R=L=J – so probably with

00:09:00.200 --> 00:09:04.360
the help of Bran’s visions, next episode,
we’re almost certainly finally gonna get

00:09:04.360 --> 00:09:08.340
confirmation of Jon’s true parentage.

00:09:08.340 --> 00:09:13.100
Then we have the final scene of the episode,
with Sansa killing Ramsay by feeding him to

00:09:13.100 --> 00:09:15.800
very dogs that he used to kill others.

00:09:15.800 --> 00:09:17.450
You could call that poetic justice.

00:09:17.450 --> 00:09:20.400
But in a weird way, Ramsay wins here.

00:09:20.400 --> 00:09:24.660
Before he dies, Ramsay tells Sansa that he’s
part of her now, and some people think that

00:09:24.660 --> 00:09:29.140
means Sansa’s pregnant or something, but
what this really means is that Ramsay changed

00:09:29.140 --> 00:09:34.390
Sansa from someone gentle and compassionate
to someone sadistic and cruel like him, because

00:09:34.390 --> 00:09:40.860
it is sadistic to have someone eaten alive
by dogs and to enjoy it, to watch it, and

00:09:40.860 --> 00:09:43.830
smile at someone else’s horrific suffering…

00:09:43.830 --> 00:09:48.350
That’s not the Stark way, that not what
Ned would have done, clean and honourable

00:09:48.350 --> 00:09:49.870
and respectful.

00:09:49.870 --> 00:09:54.570
Feeding someone to dogs, and watching it for
pleasure is exactly sort of thing Ramsay would

00:09:54.570 --> 00:09:55.570
do.

00:09:55.570 --> 00:10:00.700
By inflicting this revenge, Sansa has stooped
down to his level, she has allowed herself

00:10:00.700 --> 00:10:05.570
to be consumed by the same bloodthirst that
she hates in Ramsay, she killed him but she

00:10:05.570 --> 00:10:10.950
allowed his cruelty to become part of her
.

00:10:10.950 --> 00:10:13.440
So who rules the north now?

00:10:13.440 --> 00:10:18.430
With Rickon dead, and Bran still believed
dead, and Jon still believed a bastard, Sansa

00:10:18.430 --> 00:10:21.030
should now be the head of House Stark.

00:10:21.030 --> 00:10:23.610
But Littlefinger is the one with the power
here, right?

00:10:23.610 --> 00:10:27.970
He controls the biggest army, and we know
that he wants to rule the north.

00:10:27.970 --> 00:10:33.180
Last season, he makes a deal with Cersei to
name him Warden of the North if he takes Winterfell.

00:10:33.180 --> 00:10:37.670
So maybe Littlefinger will take Winterfell
from the Starks and rule the north himself.

00:10:37.670 --> 00:10:43.340
Or maybe he’ll wanna marry Sansa, join his
power to hers and rule the north together.

00:10:43.340 --> 00:10:47.560
Maybe that was Sansa’s plan all along, maybe
that’s why she didn’t tell Jon about the

00:10:47.560 --> 00:10:48.600
knights of the Vale.

00:10:48.600 --> 00:10:53.820
Cause if she just told Jon she had army coming,
he wouldn’t have had to rush into that losing

00:10:53.820 --> 00:10:57.580
battle, he could have just waited for the
knights of the Vale and saved thousands of

00:10:57.580 --> 00:10:59.250
northern lives.

00:10:59.250 --> 00:11:03.470
Maybe Sansa wanted this, maybe she planned
to let the armies of the north destroy each

00:11:03.470 --> 00:11:08.760
other, so she and Littlefinger could mop up
and be sure to have Winterfell to themselves.

00:11:08.760 --> 00:11:13.480
And maybe Sansa still hasn’t forgiven Littlefinger
for giving her to Ramsay, and for being a

00:11:13.480 --> 00:11:18.540
manipulative scheming creep generally, and
will kill him after taking power, leaving

00:11:18.540 --> 00:11:24.450
her in control, with all the power, as Warden,
even Queen in the north.

00:11:24.450 --> 00:11:27.570
Of course, it’s not clear if Jon will be
cool with all this.

00:11:27.570 --> 00:11:32.410
And given all the hints about him and kingship,
given the probable revelations about his parentage

00:11:32.410 --> 00:11:36.860
next episode, it may be that he’ll make
some claim as King in the North – or even

00:11:36.860 --> 00:11:38.230
of Westeros.

00:11:38.230 --> 00:11:42.870
So this could go a bunch of ways – with
Littlefinger, Sansa and Jon all vying for

00:11:42.870 --> 00:11:44.290
power.

00:11:44.290 --> 00:11:47.130
The situation in Meereen of course is clearer.

00:11:47.130 --> 00:11:50.340
With her defeat of the slavers, Dany’s power
is now unquestioned.

00:11:50.340 --> 00:11:55.600
She’s got her three dragons, her Dothraki,
her Unsullied, Second Sons, her ironborn with

00:11:55.600 --> 00:12:01.170
all their ships – Dany now has what she
needs to sail west to Westeros.

00:12:01.170 --> 00:12:04.530
The only likely complications left ia Euron.

00:12:04.530 --> 00:12:09.740
But yeah this episode was pretty awesome,
it really plays to the strengths of the show.

00:12:09.740 --> 00:12:14.510
Cause the show is sometimes bad with plot
and character, but it what does really well

00:12:14.510 --> 00:12:15.950
is spectacle.

00:12:15.950 --> 00:12:20.580
These shots of dragons above Meereen, and
the Battle of Winterfell, are stunning, and

00:12:20.580 --> 00:12:22.700
something you can never get from a book.

00:12:22.700 --> 00:12:27.140
So for all the show’s shortcomings, it is
still great TV and we are really lucky to

00:12:27.140 --> 00:12:29.860
get to see this story in both mediums.

00:12:29.860 --> 00:12:32.750
So that’s nine episodes down, one to go.

00:12:32.750 --> 00:12:36.940
Thank you all for watching so far and special
thanks to all the Patrons supporting this

00:12:36.940 --> 00:12:41.930
channel on Patreon, including Phillip Bond,
Moiraine Sedai, Mohammed Alkaabi, Johanna

00:12:41.930 --> 00:12:47.410
Kammler, mindy rossetto, Katie Murphy, Sephora
Rothschild, Jacob Zachs, Mauna Pandya, Elizabeth

00:12:47.410 --> 00:12:49.710
Frum, Michael Howie, and Dirk.

00:12:49.710 --> 00:12:50.310
Cheers.

